  "application_type_full": "Householder planning permission",
  "description": "The application seeks permission for the installation of a secure cycle store in the front garden of 8 Shardcroft Avenue, Lambeth. The proposed structure is a single-compartment unit measuring approximately 2.5 metres in width, 1 metre in depth, and 1.5 metres in height. It is constructed from a powder-coated steel frame, clad in narrow-profile timber, and topped with a planted green roof to enhance visual amenity and support local biodiversity.\n\nThe store is positioned discreetly behind the existing front boundary wall and concealed further by planting and a metal fence, ensuring minimal visibility from the street. Located adjacent to the neighbouring property at 8A, where a 2-metre-high wall provides full screening along the shared boundary, the structure has no impact on neighbouring light or outlook. The proposal offers a modest, high-quality, and environmentally responsive storage solution that supports active travel and aligns with Lambeth Council’s aspirations for sustainable residential infrastructure.\n\n",
